venv/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Source reports and generated tables.
# These are large (well over 1 GB) and are not meant to live in git: they were
# briefly routed through Git LFS, which only moves the bytes into GitHub's
# metered LFS quota instead of removing them. Both sets are regenerable —
# Reports/ from the official sources listed in In/SOURCES.md,
# Out/ by re-running the pipeline scripts — so they are simply ignored.
#
# The extensions are listed in both cases: the pipeline writes the per-table
# PDFs as .PDF and the tables as .csv, while the source reports are .pdf.
# Git patterns are case-sensitive unless core.ignorecase is set, so a lowercase
# *.pdf alone would stop matching the generated files and leave Out/ untracked
# but visible. Out/ is also ignored wholesale as the authoritative rule, except
# each year's index, database and review pages (Out/<year>/*.tsv, *.sql,
# *.sqlite, *.html), kept so a checkout has them without a re-run.
# Out/.work/ stays ignored. Directories are re-included first, because git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
Out/**
!Out/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/
!Out/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/*.tsv
!Out/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/*.sql
!Out/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/*.sqlite
!Out/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/*.html
*.pdf
*.PDF
*.csv
*.xls
*.XLS
*.xlsx
*.XLSX

# Built explorer (tools/build_site.py): regenerable from web/ and Out/.
site/
